From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yevhen Salitrynskyi <ysalitrynskyi@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 13:06:41 -0400
Subject: tests: fewer browser tests, merged into scenarios; parallel-safe;
 weak checks fixed

The tests of 2026-10-14, on the operator's word: cut the number of tests without losing
what they prove, and make the runs faster. One patch at the tip: the files are test files
touched by most patches since 0057, and fixups into each would conflict.

Browser tests that shared a setup are one scenario now, each old test a step under a
SCOPED_TRACE with its expectations kept, the state put back between steps; a test whose
checks another test already made is gone, and four the first pass deleted without a real
cover are back. Unit tests that were near-copies are one table each, true duplicates are
gone, and different behaviours stay separate tests. Weak checks were tightened where the
merge read them: a link drop below a folder's last row and on a collapsed folder, the tab
strip internals page showing the folder (with the page's Expand All), the settings page's
address loading in the profile's jar, the isolation question skipping pins and sleeping
tabs, the emptied nested folder going, a context menu's rows asserted present before they
are asserted hidden.

Parallel runs: a drag fixture keeps its window above other windows (a tab drag asks the
system which window is under each point, and a new test window is not always in front);
a pointer to the command bar is looked up again after a wait (the bar closes when its
window loses focus); a merged step that changes Spaces runs last; the typed text is
waited for before it is read.

It also holds the tests of patch 0063's evening fixes, in the files this
patch rewrote: a folder closed in part comes back in its places, whole or
one row at a time (FolderTabsTest, FolderSessionTest, TabStripModelTest),
and Restore Folder with Shift held keeps the folder in one new window.

Why: 233 browser tests took 208 s one at a time; the same checks in 103 tests take about
65 s, most of them four at a time (tooling/dev, SERIAL_BROWSER_TESTS).
Removable when: never; these are Stedding's own tests.
